# increasing_subsequence:
# CSES 1145, Increasing Subsequence (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1145), in
# our own words: from a list of numbers, some are kept, in their order, so that each
# kept number is larger than the one before it; the most numbers that can be kept.
# The input is a Scott list (corpora/library/prelude/list) of binary naturals
# (corpora/library/binary/natural) and the answer a binary natural. Part of the
# CSES port's third batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: the list of all subsequences of the list
# is built (the subsequences of a number followed by the others are the
# subsequences of the others, and the same with the number put in front), and the
# greatest length among those whose numbers strictly increase is taken. Its reading
# is exponential in the length of the list even under tabling, since the 2^n
# subsequences are built and checked; the replacement the family asks for is
# patience sorting, which keeps for each length the least number that ends an
# increasing subsequence of that length and finds the place of a number by binary
# search, about n log n steps, on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only: its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces
# to V, the canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since
# subsequences consumes the finite list and every other recursion consumes a
# finite list; the branches that a Scott boolean discards are never read. The
# program calls no subtraction. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable
# equations for the contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than binary_maximum _
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self numbers
    . numbers (cons nil nil)
      λ head tail
      . ( λ rest
          . append (map (cons head) rest) rest
        ) λ. self tail
  )
λ subsequences
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self numbers
    . numbers true
      λ head tail
      . tail true
        λ next _
        . binary_less_than head next (self tail) false
  )
λ increasing
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λself count items. items count λ_ tail. self (merge_binary_increment count) tail
  )
λ count_from
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self most subsequence_list
    . subsequence_list most
      λ subsequence rest
      . self (increasing subsequence (binary_maximum most (count_from binary_zero subsequence)) most) rest
  )
λ longest
. (λtuple. tuple λnumbers. longest binary_zero (subsequences numbers))
λ increasing_subsequence
. export increasing_subsequence
